{
  "$comment": [
    "The destinations the fixture provider knows about.",
    "",
    "This is the one file in data/ whose contents are true: the opening-hours",
    "advice, the markets, the day trips. It is here rather than in TypeScript so",
    "that both runtimes read the same rows, and so that adding a city is a data",
    "change a person can make without touching an agent loop.",
    "",
    "`aliases` is how free text resolves. It used to be a separate map, and a",
    "destination could end up in one and not the other; a city that cannot be",
    "named is a city that does not exist, so the names live on the record.",
    "",
    "`places` is what a map needs and nothing else: the city centre, each named",
    "area and each highlight, as {name, kind, lat, lon}. Real coordinates, to",
    "about a street block — these are centroids somebody can check, not surveyed",
    "points, and the file says so rather than implying a precision it does not",
    "have. A day trip sits where it really is, which is why Toledo is an hour",
    "southwest of Madrid on the map instead of inside it.",
    "",
    "A generated city has none. Inventing a fare is the sin this app refuses",
    "everywhere else, and a coordinate is a fare with worse consequences: it puts",
    "somebody's hotel in the sea. No coordinates means no map, which is the right",
    "answer rather than a missing feature."
  ],
